#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166437 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "276898e7-57a4-5ca6-8df7-99fd318a2702" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Decoupled System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "a19f597d-f584-57b3-9e67-cb4cea07c876" :question/math-academy-id "e-21120" :question/problem "Which of the following systems of linear ODEs are decoupled?\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=7{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "A *decoupled system* consists of equations depending on only one variable, such as\n\n$$\nx'_i(t) = \\lambda_i x_i(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda_i$ is a constant. This means that we can solve each equation independently. \n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our systems.\n\n- System I is *not* decoupled because some of its equations depend on more than one variable. For example, $x'_1(t) = 4x_1(t) + 2x_2(t)$ depends on $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t).$\n\n- System II is decoupled since its equations depend on only one variable each. Indeed, $x'_1(t) = -3x_1(t)$ depends on only $x_1(t)$ and $x'_2(t) = 7x_2(t)$ depends on only $x_2(t).$\n\n- System III is *not* decoupled because, for example, the first equation depends on $x_2(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166438 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce35e5a9-2444-5e5f-9463-5a4d54496d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Decoupled Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "83ebd59d-883f-510a-9bc9-035b3088a43c" :question/math-academy-id "e-21123" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-6{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a decoupled system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/17657d7db880fc0ababc24511039a9d7446952f7521e31ae3351adbb6b28ee61.png)\nthe formula for the general solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/44a286f1a4c15598038f38cdb4140534bac24caacb36f32ee4ef9cbe05b3e5e1.png)\n\nFirst, we write our differential equation in matrix form:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/d9b9ac7fc20d076110f99476fc48d3c00c4206dc37fb2a929893fcbbb77d6526.png)\n\nSince the matrix of the differential system is diagonal, the system is decoupled. \n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/4f7cfa979200fccf811a7e0d9a633b7919b33b7740c635a921b75ad09995e700.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166439 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cec0e48f-9fbb-5ada-b7fd-0d389d1b7438" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for a Decoupled Linear System of First-Order ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "f5136df2-fcf6-5f64-aeda-f14a91231788" :question/math-academy-id "e-21124" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/5cc29f7492fded69b4100e10329c831cca0734a29966cd1aac2e8ad017636719.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{1t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)})}^{t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of $c_1$ and $c_2$ using the initial value $\\mathbf{x}(0).$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{0} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+(-1)[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce35e5a9-2444-5e5f-9463-5a4d54496d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Decoupled Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "297dfcf0-0119-5f66-a683-25789f86a54d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=c[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,c\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353913} {:answer/id #uuid "ab49702a-2642-56d3-aebb-ae2e7031417d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353914} {:answer/id #uuid "6dccdf57-89ca-5905-92d2-f16e9c464c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-6[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{c}_{1}t}+6[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{c}_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353915} {:answer/id #uuid "b9294248-1b58-5581-9bfc-91dcfc70d0de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=c[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-6t},\\,c\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353916} {:answer/id #uuid "956c74c4-f3c3-5e46-851f-5a6053014623" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab49702a-2642-56d3-aebb-ae2e7031417d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353914} :answer-field/id #uuid "1abba9be-df64-52b3-8203-fdf82a8a9100" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5fe31ca3-9692-5c8b-b936-2c7c902b4cf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-167507" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the matrix differential equation $\\,{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]x(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a decoupled system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the matrix of our differential equation is diagonal, the system is decoupled. \n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353918 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce35e5a9-2444-5e5f-9463-5a4d54496d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Decoupled Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae2e75be-03e5-5a88-b3b4-0b2e5eb02c25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t/2},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353920} {:answer/id #uuid "731598dc-e704-5dd1-970d-65b85f9d8176" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{c}_{1}t}+2[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{c}_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353921} {:answer/id #uuid "4f8b755b-f43f-5afc-88ee-a1feae4da0b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t/2}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353922} {:answer/id #uuid "85ffdaf7-00f7-5afa-950b-2a5620c8d2d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=c[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,c\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353923} {:answer/id #uuid "a868afd6-e3b7-5d0f-a22d-ecec100de2be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=c[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t/2},\\,c\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f8b755b-f43f-5afc-88ee-a1feae4da0b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t/2}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353922} :answer-field/id #uuid "516e7593-61b8-5bfb-a0bf-5fc11198e00a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97377a38-6ced-5c8a-940c-b93e09b089f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-167514" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations\n${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "Given a decoupled system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write our differential equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSince the matrix of the differential system is diagonal, the system is decoupled. \n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t/2}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cec0e48f-9fbb-5ada-b7fd-0d389d1b7438" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial 